endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 100 0 R
/T (Wearable emergency hardware is typically powered by a rechargeable single-cell Lithium-ion or LiPo pouch battery \(nominal 3.7V\). During discharge, the battery voltage varies from 4.2V when fully charged down to 3.0V when depleted. A conventional Low-Dropout \(LDO\) regulator cannot operate when the battery falls below 3.3V plus its dropout voltage, leaving a substantial portion of the battery's energy unused. Conversely, a pure step-down \(buck\) regulator fails below 3.3V, while a pure boost regulator cannot regulate when the battery is at 4.2V.)
/E (Wearable emergency hardware is typically powered by a rechargeable single-cell Lithium-ion or LiPo pouch battery \(nominal 3.7V\). During discharge, the battery voltage varies from 4.2V when fully charged down to 3.0V when depleted. A conventional Low-Dropout \(LDO\) regulator cannot operate when the battery falls below 3.3V plus its dropout voltage, leaving a substantial portion of the battery's energy unused. Conversely, a pure step-down \(buck\) regulator fails below 3.3V, while a pure boost regulator cannot regulate when the battery is at 4.2V.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 100 0 R
/T (To solve this, the circuit incorporates the Texas Instruments TPS63001 \(U2\), a high-efficiency, low-noise synchronous buck-boost DC-DC converter. The TPS63001 seamlessly transitions between buck mode \(when battery > 3.3V\) and boost mode \(when battery < 3.3V\), delivering a rock-solid, regulated +3.3V output rail capable of delivering up to 800 mA of current. Key supporting passives include:)
/E (To solve this, the circuit incorporates the Texas Instruments TPS63001 \(U2\), a high-efficiency, low-noise synchronous buck-boost DC-DC converter. The TPS63001 seamlessly transitions between buck mode \(when battery > 3.3V\) and boost mode \(when battery < 3.3V\), delivering a rock-solid, regulated +3.3V output rail capable of delivering up to 800 mA of current. Key supporting passives include:)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
