556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 110 0 R
/T (A critical phase in modern electronic hardware design is 3D electromechanical verification. Using the integrated KiCad 3D Raytracing Viewer, accurate STEP and VRML 3D component models were rendered on the virtual board. This allows the hardware designer to verify physical component heights, lead forming, connector clearance, and mechanical housing compatibility before spending budget on PCB fabrication.)
/E (A critical phase in modern electronic hardware design is 3D electromechanical verification. Using the integrated KiCad 3D Raytracing Viewer, accurate STEP and VRML 3D component models were rendered on the virtual board. This allows the hardware designer to verify physical component heights, lead forming, connector clearance, and mechanical housing compatibility before spending budget on PCB fabrication.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 110 0 R
/T (1. Vertical Component Profiles & Enclosure Fit: The tallest component on the board is the cylindrical plastic body of the BC547 transistor \(Q1\) and the piezo buzzer \(BZ1, ~5.5 mm height\), followed by the through-hole JST PH connector \(P1\) and 4-pin OLED header \(J1\). All discrete surface-mount passives \(0805 resistors, capacitors, inductor\) and ICs \(ESP32, TPS63001, MPU-6050\) maintain a very low profile \(< 1.5 mm\). This guarantees that the complete PCB assembly easily fits inside a slim, compact 3D-printed enclosure or wearable wrist casing.)
/E (1. Vertical Component Profiles & Enclosure Fit: The tallest component on the board is the cylindrical plastic body of the BC547 transistor \(Q1\) and the piezo buzzer \(BZ1, ~5.5 mm height\), followed by the through-hole JST PH connector \(P1\) and 4-pin OLED header \(J1\). All discrete surface-mount passives \(0805 resistors, capacitors, inductor\) and ICs \(ESP32, TPS63001, MPU-6050\) maintain a very low profile \(< 1.5 mm\). This guarantees that the complete PCB assembly easily fits inside a slim, compact 3D-printed enclosure or wearable wrist casing.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 110 0 R
/T (2. Connector Accessibility: The battery input connector \(P1\) is oriented with its insertion shroud opening toward the left border, enabling easy battery replacement. Similarly, the OLED header \(J1\) faces downward along the bottom edge, ensuring that the display ribbon does not obstruct the central buttons, sensor, or the ESP32 antenna.)
/E (2. Connector Accessibility: The battery input connector \(P1\) is oriented with its insertion shroud opening toward the left border, enabling easy battery replacement. Similarly, the OLED header \(J1\) faces downward along the bottom edge, ensuring that the display ribbon does not obstruct the central buttons, sensor, or the ESP32 antenna.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
