/T (1. Single-Pass Reflow Soldering: It allows the PCB to be assembled in a single reflow soldering pass, dramatically slashing fabrication and pick-and-place setup costs. A double-sided SMD board requires two stencil printings, two pick-and-place runs, and two passes through the reflow oven \(with glue or double-sided soldering profile\), doubling assembly cost.)
/E (1. Single-Pass Reflow Soldering: It allows the PCB to be assembled in a single reflow soldering pass, dramatically slashing fabrication and pick-and-place setup costs. A double-sided SMD board requires two stencil printings, two pick-and-place runs, and two passes through the reflow oven \(with glue or double-sided soldering profile\), doubling assembly cost.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
