710 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 115 0 R
/T (The process of assigning footprints in Cvpcb highlighted how component package sizes directly dictate board density. Balancing the use of easily solderable 0805 passives with ultra-miniature fine-pitch ICs \(like the QFN-24 MPU-6050 and VSON-10 TPS63001\) demonstrated real-world trade-offs between board miniaturization and ease of assembly. During the layout phase, routing power traces with adequate copper width while preserving a low-impedance ground return plane taught me the practical importance of return current paths and high di/dt switching loop containment.)
/E (The process of assigning footprints in Cvpcb highlighted how component package sizes directly dictate board density. Balancing the use of easily solderable 0805 passives with ultra-miniature fine-pitch ICs \(like the QFN-24 MPU-6050 and VSON-10 TPS63001\) demonstrated real-world trade-offs between board miniaturization and ease of assembly. During the layout phase, routing power traces with adequate copper width while preserving a low-impedance ground return plane taught me the practical importance of return current paths and high di/dt switching loop containment.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
