1357 0 obj
<<
/Title (In professional PCB design methodology, starting directly with component layout on a blank board is extremely prone to error. Schematic capture in KiCad Eeschema / eSim establishes the logical and electrical truth of the circuit first. Every component's electrical function, pin numbering, logical net names, power distribution nets, and ground returns are explicitly wired and systematically checked using the Electrical Rules Checker \(ERC\). Once verified, the schematic generates a netlist file that dictates exact pad-to-pad connectivity in the PCB editor. This netlist guides the physical layout with a 'ratsnest' \(unrouted connection lines\), ensuring that no electrical traces are accidentally omitted, shorted, or incorrectly routed during board design.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1256 0 R
/Next 1358 0 R
>>
endobj
