/Title (Wearable emergency hardware is typically powered by a rechargeable single-cell Lithium-ion or LiPo pouch battery \(nominal 3.7V\). During discharge, the battery voltage varies from 4.2V when fully charged down to 3.0V when depleted. A conventional Low-Dropout \(LDO\) regulator cannot operate when the battery falls below 3.3V plus its dropout voltage, leaving a substantial portion of the battery's energy unused. Conversely, a pure step-down \(buck\) regulator fails below 3.3V, while a pure boost regulator cannot regulate when the battery is at 4.2V.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1480 0 R
/Next 1536 0 R
