1664 0 obj
<<
/Title (1. Western Zone \(User Interface & Connectors\): Houses the distress push-button \(SW1\), the JST battery connector \(P1\), and the tri-color LED status cluster \(D1, D2, D3 with resistors R5, R6, R7\). Positioning P1 at the left edge guarantees unobstructed cable entry. SW1 is easily accessible by the user's thumb, and the LEDs are aligned along the edge for clear panel visibility.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1636 0 R
/Prev 1652 0 R
/Next 1676 0 R
>>
endobj
1665 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. Eastern Zone \(Microcontroller Core & RF Antenna\): The ESP32-WROOM-32 module \(U1\) occupies the eastern section. Critically, the integrated meandering inverted-F PCB antenna extends past the board's right edge into a dedicated Antenna Keep-Out Zone. The 4-pin OLED header \(J1\) is located at the bottom edge, allowing an external display ribbon to plug in without crossing the high-speed RF antenna.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1636 0 R
/Prev 1676 0 R
/Next 1653 0 R
>>
endobj
